{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"79f62e4ab4eefd9e5c8224b3dca38585561290f45174a6acb9d42ff0e8075dba","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AAAgQQAAQEEAADBBAACgQAAAoEEAAKhBAAC4QQAAIEKdDTRBzv45QQ87PEEAAMBA","role":"input"},{"binding":1,"initial_bytes_b64":"q6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6s=","role":"in_out"}],"case_id":"c7af3834065a2c9e0139ffb641ec86ce6d7eb11bc1601c4a34a102b0f522b722","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[1,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[1,1,1]},"entry":"TonemappingRange_float4","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"average-three-channels-left-to-right-before-widening","output":{"binding":1,"kind":"buffer","length":68,"offset":0},"rationale":"The first three channels take the rebalancing branch, which collapses the bounds to 10 and 23 and replaces the average by the mean of the three supplied averages -- a three-term sum the shader spells left to right and then divides by three, and neither the adds nor the divide carries permission to reassociate or to use a reciprocal. The three averages are chosen so grouping the sum the other way lands on a different float, and the second stage widens that difference by four and a half before the upper bound is stored, while the lower bound clamps and says so. The fourth channel keeps its own average and rides a separate, exactly representable widening, so it pins the untouched lane.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"7a0cf0e338c2b534cc2abff41e53dc21b079be989bb81ba985514164c25121e8","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AACAPwAAAEAAAEBAAACAQAAAekQAAPpEAIA7RQAAekUAAABA","role":"input"},{"binding":1,"initial_bytes_b64":"q6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6s=","role":"output"}],"case_id":"e875ced88025db9d67cbc6bc822e5cfe5ce08a7070b89d68a2656d62e3eee549","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[8,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[8,1,1]},"entry":"uniform_member_helper_twice","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"evaluate-one-uniform-member-from-two-call-sites","output":{"binding":1,"kind":"buffer","length":32,"offset":0},"rationale":"A `constant Params&` whose first member is handed to a NOINLINE helper from TWO call sites. Metal's `constant` space carries whole uniform structs, so a helper that takes one member of one is routinely called again -- and only one byte cursor per callee parameter can be recorded, so the emitter used to refuse the second call site's cursor by refusing every callee with more than one call site. Both call sites here name the same member, so no cursor can conflict, but the helper still read its whole coefficient struct as zero: ten loads folded to `OpConstantNull` with spirv-val happy. The helper is two blocks on purpose -- a one-block leaf is inlined before the call path is ever reached. Buffer 0 holds a = (1, 2, 3, 4), then a decoy b = (1000, 2000, 3000, 4000), then scale = 2. The helper evaluates 4x^3 + 3x^2 + 2x + 1 at x = gid, and odd threads add its value at gid + 1, so both call sites are live and the second one is the one the old gate refused. Every coefficient, every power of an integer gid up to 8, and every partial sum is an exact binary32 integer below 2^24, so fast-math reassociation and fma contraction cannot move the answer: (2, 118, 98, 910, 626, 3142, 1970, 7582). The three failure modes are all separated. Coefficients read as zero give all zeros; the decoy member read instead gives values a thousand times larger; a cursor dropped only on the second call site leaves the four ODD lanes short.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"7a2f3f3a94f7c5accfb88791b1d475065f5467501d09f74d9c9ce7b9e0e93631","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"codex:gpt-5.6-sol","buffers":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AAAAAAAAAAA=","role":"input"}],"case_id":"a47318c70a76b40aba05abb907fcc7e0f3ec5d6f759b7359959af0516f1908af","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[256,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[256,1,1]},"entry":"inputStreamTrackingAreas","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"fixed-array-eight-simdgroup-maximum","output":{"binding":4,"dimensions":[1,1,1],"kind":"texture","origin":[0,0,0]},"rationale":"One complete 256-thread workgroup forms exactly eight 32-lane SIMD groups, so every shared reduction slot is initialized before the barrier. The kernel structurally selects element zero of the fixed texture array; its pixel-coordinate clamp-to-edge sampler makes every gather return uint 7, and thread zero writes the exact uint4 maximum.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[{"binding":0,"elements":[{"bytes_b64":"BwAAAA==","dimensions":[1,1,1]},{"bytes_b64":"CwAAAA==","dimensions":[1,1,1]}],"format":"r32_uint","role":"input","texture_type":"d2"}],"textures":[{"binding":4,"dimensions":[1,1,1],"format":"rgba32_uint","initial_bytes_b64":"q6urq6urq6urq6urq6urqw==","role":"output","texture_type":"d2"}],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
