{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"7ab814aea6e10dcea708f8a3e0801cf020d90f525bec1504bcd6f2aa0fd00c2c","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"AAEAAgEBAQICAQICAwEDAgQBBAIFAQUCBgEGAgcBBwI=","role":"input"},{"binding":1,"initial_bytes_b64":"zc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc0=","role":"in_out"}],"case_id":"d94b2497b6a076c0561f5634249679326198d4b399e3afc3c15d7bb9d1db070b","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[8,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[8,1,1]},"entry":"subword_reinterpret_roundtrip","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"read-and-write-a-subword-vector-through-a-word-pointer","output":{"binding":1,"kind":"buffer","length":128,"offset":0},"rationale":"A subword vector read from, and written back through, a WORD pointer -- the *(device ushort2*) reinterpret Metal code writes whenever it treats a uint buffer as pairs of halves. The SPIR-V pointer keeps its declared uint pointee, so both directions are equal-width reinterprets of the VALUE and are the same two instructions in mirror image: the load is OpLoad of the word plus OpBitcast up to ushort2, the store is OpBitcast down to the word plus OpStore. The emitter must therefore accept the same pointee/object pairs on both sides; a store arm narrower than the load arm refuses to write back what the load just read. in[i] packs two DIFFERENT halves, 0x0100+i low and 0x0200+i high, so a swapped lane pair is visible as a value and not just as a width. The first two rows extract each half through ordinary word stores, which pins which half is which; the third row is the reinterpret store itself, writing the halves back SWAPPED as one word. The fourth row is never written and must still hold its 0xCD fill: a store that took the narrowing path would leave half of out[16+i] at the fill byte, and a store that overshot its word would land in row three. Each lane writes one slot no other lane touches, so there is no race.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"7aea7d2046a18cf42c114b1589f4869e1ede17023d76e59fd51f69a30dec9e2b","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"buffers":[],"case_id":"3a1a473b5011b86dece98ca33021cc837294f652c4077294bb8ccc80050b4de4","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"draw":{"instance_count":1,"primitive":"triangle","vertex_count":3,"vertex_start":0},"entry":"fullScreenSetDepthToZero","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"vertex-position-depth-zero","output":{"dimensions":[2,2],"index":0,"kind":"render_target","origin":[0,0]},"rationale":"The vertex entry preserves authored x/y, forces clip-space z to zero and w to one, and the typed position observer captures the resulting full-coverage triangle.","render_targets":[{"dimensions":[2,2],"format":"rgba32_float","index":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"q6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urqw=="}],"samplers":[],"stage":"vertex","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[{"bytes_b64":"AACAvwAAgL8AAAAAAACAPwAAQEAAAIC/AAAAAAAAgD8AAIC/AABAQAAAAAAAAIA/","format":"float4","location":0,"stride":16},{"bytes_b64":"AACAPgAAAD8AAIA+AAAAPwAAgD4AAAA/","format":"float2","location":1,"stride":8}],"vertex_observation":{"kind":"position"},"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"7b0c081babad00ed84f6821e2b756d0fae751550c69133705f9f8e247f863105","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"q6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6s=","role":"in_out"},{"binding":1,"bytes_b64":"AADIQgAkdEnbD8lKAADIQgAkdMnbD8lK3A/JStwPyco=","role":"input"}],"case_id":"179b6aa6c7fb35fecec313ecf56c08cd2d3f4c55e2ff87176a99695120882e7b","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[1,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[1,1,1]},"entry":"kernel_fast_trig_range","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"fast-trig-across-the-whole-evaluated-range","output":{"binding":0,"kind":"buffer","length":32,"offset":0},"rationale":"fast::sin and fast::cos on float3 and on a scalar, at the arguments that separate Metal's own reduction from a hand-rolled one. Six of the eight are the correctly rounded float32 sine or cosine of the argument -- derived here in float64 and rounded once, 0 ULP against the observation at every one -- and the remaining two are the flush.\n\nThe first lane is the point of the case. This translator used to reduce the argument itself, x - trunc(x / 2pi) * 2pi, before handing it to the trig call. That expression rounds twice, so the residue it produces carries the absolute error of a number the size of x rather than of the residue, and at x = 100 the answer came back 38 ULP from Metal's. Metal reduces more carefully than that, and so does the MSL sin the emitted GLSL call becomes, so the reduction was pure loss; it is gone, and this lane is what says so. The 1e6 lanes, in both signs, are two decades further out and would move further still.\n\nThe third lane of each vector is 6588397.5, which is float(pi/2) times 2^22 -- the largest magnitude the hardware still evaluates, bisected on this repository's reference GPU. The two scalars are the very next float in each direction, 6588398 and its negative, where both functions answer exactly zero. A lowering that dropped the flush would return an ordinary sine there instead of zero, and one that flushed a binade early would return zero for the vector's third lane.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
